# Instructions and configuration snippets for additional components

## 1. Keycloak Configuration
To send Keycloak logs to syslog (so they are aggregated into `/var/log/syslog` and rotated hourly), modify `/opt/keycloak/conf/keycloak.conf` to append `syslog`:

```properties
# Add syslog to log handlers
log=console,file,syslog

2. systemd-journald Forwarding to Syslog (for rsyslog integration)

To ensure systemd service logs (such as Payara running under a systemd unit or other services) are properly forwarded to syslog for rsyslog to capture:

Edit /etc/systemd/journald.conf:

[Journal]
# Ensure journal logs are forwarded to syslog
ForwardToSyslog=yes

After modifying, restart journald:

sudo systemctl restart systemd-journald

3. Hourly Cron / Trigger Deployment

Instead of using a wildcard cron rule that runs every minute, deploy the script to run strictly on the hour.

You can configure this by placing a cron file under /etc/cron.d/upload-s3:

# Run the upload script every hour on the hour as root
0 * * * * root /opt/upload-s3

Alternatively, symlink or copy the script directly to /etc/cron.hourly/:

sudo cp scripts/upload-s3 /etc/cron.hourly/upload-s3
sudo chmod +x /etc/cron.hourly/upload-s3
